\": \"PASS\",\n    \"textIssues\": [],\n    \"choiceIssues\": [],\n    \"answerIssues\": [],\n    \"explanationIssues\": [],\n    \"figureIssues\": [],\n    \"sourceIssues\": [],\n    \"verifiedEvidence\": [\n      \"Checked the question text against the official page (footer -7- / T2-D 010) word for word, including 常に(ア)負荷を接続, 一次電流（負荷電流）が流れている状態では, 二次回路を(イ)してはならない, 大きな(ウ)が発生し(エ)が過大, and 被測定線路に(オ)に接続. The wording matches.\",\n      \"Options (1)-(5) match the official table for all five blanks (ア)-(オ). (1) high impedance / short circuit / voltage / iron loss / series. (2) low / short circuit / induced current / copper loss / parallel. (3) high / short circuit / induced current / copper loss / series. (4) low / open / voltage / iron loss / series. (5) high / open / voltage / copper loss / parallel.\",\n      \"The official answer (4) matches the manifest's answer=4.\",\n      \"Main explanation: if the secondary is opened, the cancelling magnetomotive force disappears and the primary current acts as excitation current. The core saturates, a high voltage appears on the secondary, and iron loss becomes excessive. A current transformer with primary terminals is connected in series with the measured line. The cause-and-effect chain is correct.\",\n      \"Why each wrong option is wrong: (1) (ア) and (イ) are wrong; the other three are correct. (2) only (ア) is correct. (3) only (オ) is correct. (5) (ア), (エ) and (オ) are wrong; (イ) and (ウ) are correct. I checked every blank of every option against the table, and all of this is accurate.\",\n      \"No figure is needed, and figureUrls is empty. This is consistent.\",\n      \"officialReferenceUrls is empty, so there are no independent claims to verify.\",\n      \"reviewedFromPage=[10] matches T2-D 010 on the attached original.\"\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3869,"cache_read_input_tokens":162576,"cache_